From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivo Nunes <ivo@nunes.uk>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:43:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: Name the user's profile folder after the user when
 asked.

Wheelio: CrossOver calls every user "crossover" (Hack 12735), and
CX_REPORT_REAL_USERNAME turns that off for GetUserNameW but not for the
profile folder, which stays C:\users\crossover. Games run as "steamuser",
as on Proton, because that is the folder Steam Cloud maps Windows saves
into, so the profile folder follows GetUserNameW.

Origin: Wheelio.
---
 dlls/shell32/shellpath.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/shell32/shellpath.c b/dlls/shell32/shellpath.c
index adfa296..720413c 100644
--- a/dlls/shell32/shellpath.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shellpath.c
@@ -2632,9 +2632,12 @@ static HRESULT _SHExpandEnvironmentStrings(LPCWSTR szSrc, LPWSTR szDest)
         }
         else if (!wcsnicmp(szTemp, L"%USERPROFILE%", lstrlenW(L"%USERPROFILE%")))
         {
-            /* CrossOver Hack 12735 */
-            static const WCHAR userName[] = {'c','r','o','s','s','o','v','e','r',0};
+            /* CrossOver Hack 12735, which GetUserNameW keeps unless
+             * CX_REPORT_REAL_USERNAME is set */
+            WCHAR userName[257] = L"crossover";
+            DWORD userNameLen = ARRAY_SIZE(userName);
 
+            GetUserNameW(userName, &userNameLen);
             lstrcpyW(szDest, szProfilesPrefix);
             PathAppendW(szDest, userName);
             PathAppendW(szDest, szTemp + lstrlenW(L"%USERPROFILE%"));
